"""Rebuild the NCC offering/campaign report from canonical costs and prices."""
from pathlib import Path
import json, html, hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def load(n):return json.loads((R/n).read_text())
def save(n,d):(R/n).write_text(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
p=load('pricing_results.json');rows={x['id']:x for x in p['products']};campaign=load('ncc_1982_campaign.json');team=load('team_development_program.json')
ids=[x for x in campaign['offering_refs'] if x.startswith(('device.','software.'))]+[x['id'] for x in campaign['packages']]
review={'as_of':'1982-06-15','headline':campaign['headline'],'basis':'Engineering recurring-cost estimates, not supplier quotations or measured production yields. Nominal USD before tax.','pricing_method':p['policy']['formula'],'comparator_limitation':'No verified like-for-like June 1982 comparator for these new products; apply existing 25% contribution/net-revenue fallback. This is not a claim of equal market-discount percentages.','products':[{'id':i,'name':rows[i]['name'],**rows[i]['snapshots']['1982']} for i in ids],'team_launch_price':rows['software.aion_development_team']['launch_snapshot'],'team_1982_price':rows['software.aion_development_team']['snapshots']['1982'],'campaign_budget_usd':campaign['budget_total_usd'],'integration_status':'New unit economics and staged campaign plan are authoritative. Existing sales, investment and ROI projections predate this revision and must not be interpreted as incorporating the new products, subsidy or campaign. No unsupported volume uplift is introduced.','source_sha256':{n:hashlib.sha256((R/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for n in ['manufacturing_costs.json','pricing_results.json','ncc_1982_inputs.json','ncc_1982_campaign.json','team_development_program.json']}}
save('ncc_1982_review.json',review)
esc=html.escape;money=lambda v:f'${v:,.2f}'
trs=''.join(f'<tr><th scope="row">{esc(x["name"])}</th><td>{money(x["manufacturing_cost_usd"])}</td><td>{money(x["retail_price_usd"])}</td><td>{money(x["computerland_fee_usd"])}</td><td>{money(x["unit_profit_usd"])}</td></tr>' for x in review['products'])
budget=''.join(f'<tr><td>{esc(x["period"])}</td><th scope="row">{esc(x["id"].replace("_"," "))}</th><td>{esc(x["basis"])}</td><td>{money(x["usd"])}</td></tr>' for x in campaign['budget_rows'])
li=lambda xs:'<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+esc(x)+'</li>' for x in xs)+'</ul>'
ts=review['team_1982_price']
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>NCC 1982 — {esc(campaign['headline'])}</title><style>body{{font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1120px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#172435;background:#fafafa}}h1{{font-size:2.8rem;line-height:1.1;max-width:850px}}h2{{margin-top:2.5rem}}a{{color:#145eaa}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.92rem;background:white}}th,td{{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd4dd;text-align:left}}td{{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}}.table{{overflow-x:auto}}.callout{{padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #117b85;background:#eef7f6}}small{{color:#435569}}nav{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px}}</style><script type="application/json" id="report-metadata">{{"source":"ncc_1982_review.json"}}</script></head><body><nav><a href="index.html">Project</a><a href="timeline.html">Timeline</a><a href="pricing.html">Price matrix</a><a href="manufacturing-costs.html">Manufacturing costs</a></nav><p>NCC · 7–10 June 1982 · Houston</p><h1>{esc(campaign['headline'])}</h1><p><strong>{esc(campaign['subheadline'])}</strong></p><p>{esc(campaign['availability'])}</p><h2>June offering</h2><p>Color Pro 14 and the 64 KiB card add 640×400 at 2 bpp and 640×200 at 4 bpp, retaining previous functions and the bounded scanline palette list. Logix Mouse has two buttons and two rollers. CP/M and AIONix TUI updates support standard controls; Entertainment Suite teaches pointing through Sudoku, Solitaire, Spider and FreeCell.</p><p>The professional extension supplies 128 KiB, 800×600 at 2 bpp, a 2D blitter/line engine and Mono Pro 17. It displays four shades selected from 16 grayscale levels. June hardware availability supports Autodesk's November target.</p><p>{esc(campaign['software_update_policy'])}</p><h2>15 June manufacturing and retail assessment</h2><p>Costs include itemized components, yield, assembly/test, manuals, packaging and logistics. Engineering, masks, tooling, capital and marketing are separate. No credible equivalent comparator was established, so new offers use the existing 25% contribution on net revenue fallback: retail = cost ÷ (0.75 × 0.75), with a 25% dealer fee. Supplier quotes and electrical qualification remain outstanding.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Offering</th><th>Recurring cost</th><th>Retail</th><th>Dealer fee</th><th>Unit contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody>{trs}</tbody></table></div><p>Packages and their components are alternative purchases; never sum both. Host computers, installation and training are excluded from upgrade prices. {esc(campaign['office_configuration'])}</p><h2>COMDEX 1981 Team Edition: rapid adoption</h2><div class="callout"><strong>{money(ts['retail_price_usd'])}</strong> from the November 1981 launch, down 50% from the frozen $1,490.45 reference (cent rounding). One server and four concurrent developer sessions; hardware separate. Original 20-hour onboarding and 12-hour first-year support remain included.</div><p>June 1982 delivery cost is {money(ts['manufacturing_cost_usd'])}; the baseline dealer fee is {money(ts['computerland_fee_usd'])}, leaving {money(ts['revenue_after_fee_usd'])} and a <strong>{money(-ts['unit_profit_usd'])} loss per licence</strong>. Direct sales at the same retail would lose {money(ts['manufacturing_cost_usd']-ts['retail_price_usd'])} before any extra direct-selling cost. This is the approved adoption subsidy, not a positive-margin price. November cost uses the disclosed June-1982 proxy; June 1981 remains prelaunch.</p><h2>Presentation and booth</h2>{li(campaign['presentation'])}<p><strong>{esc(campaign['hands_on_invitation'])}</strong> — the hands-on invitation.</p>{li([x['name']+': '+x['demo']+' '+x['conversion'] for x in campaign['booth_zones']])}<h2>Campaign schedule and provision</h2><p>April–May preparation and press previews; June NCC launch; June–July dealer/Academy sessions; August–September measured customer examples and professional beta work. October–November follow-up uses the separately scoped Autodesk COMDEX programme.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Activity</th><th>Planning basis</th><th>Budget</th></tr></thead><tbody>{budget}</tbody></table></div><p>Subtotal {money(campaign['budget_subtotal_usd'])}; 15% contingency {money(campaign['contingency_usd'])}; total staged provision <strong>{money(campaign['budget_total_usd'])}</strong>. These are scenario allowances, not vendor quotes or actual spending.</p><p>{esc(campaign['financial_boundary'])}</p><h2>Evidence and measurement</h2>{li(campaign['metrics'])}<p>{esc(campaign['followup'])}</p>{li(campaign['claim_controls'])}<p>{esc(review['integration_status'])}</p><p><a href="{campaign['conference']['date_source']}">Contemporary NCC advertisement</a> · <a href="ncc_1982_review.json">Review JSON</a> · <a href="ncc_1982_campaign.json">Campaign plan</a> · <a href="ncc_1982_inputs.json">Itemized cost assumptions</a> · <a href="team_development_program.json">Team programme</a></p></body></html>'''
(R/'ncc-1982.html').write_text(page)
print('Built NCC review JSON and HTML.')
